      "text": "Zone B - Wards 5, 6 & 7 (https://www.concordnh.gov/DocumentCenter/View/26835/CSD---Zone-B-Wards-5-6-7)\n【turn680322view0】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.concordnh.gov/DocumentCenter/View/26835/CSD---Zone-B-Wards-5-6-7\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 15\nL0@P0: BALLOT QUESTION\nL1@P0: Shall the Concord School District authorize the Concord School Board to market and sell the former\nL2@P0: Dewey School property, currently serving as the Concord School District’s central office located at 38\nL3@P0: Liberty Street, Concord, NH, in such manner (whether by bid, auction or broker listing) and on such\nL4@P0: terms, conditions, and price as it deems in the best interest of the District, with said sale subject to the\nL5@P0: District’s compliance with the statutory right of first refusal provision pertaining to charter schools in RSA\nL6@P0: 194:61?\nL7@P0: YES\nL8@P0: NO\nL9@P0: BOARD OF EDUCATION\nL10@P0: Three Year Term Vote for not more than 1\nL11@P0: DON BRUEGGEMANN\nL12@P0: LIZ BOUCHER\nL13@P0: (Write-in)\nL14@P0: SAMPLE BALLOT\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZone C - Wards 8, 9 & 10 (https://www.concordnh.gov/DocumentCenter/View/26836/CSD---Zone-C-Wards-8-9-10)\n【turn680322view1】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.concordnh.gov/DocumentCenter/View/26836/CSD---Zone-C-Wards-8-9-10\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 15\nL0@P0: BALLOT QUESTION\nL1@P0: Shall the Concord School District authorize the Concord School Board to market and sell the former\nL2@P0: Dewey School property, currently serving as the Concord School District’s central office located at 38\nL3@P0: Liberty Street, Concord, NH, in such manner (whether by bid, auction or broker listing) and on such\nL4@P0: terms, conditions, and price as it deems in the best interest of the District, with said sale subject to the\nL5@P0: District’s compliance with the statutory right of first refusal provision pertaining to charter schools in RSA\nL6@P0: 194:61?\nL7@P0: YES\nL8@P0: NO\nL9@P0: BOARD OF EDUCATION\nL10@P0: Three Year Term Vote for not more than 1\nL11@P0: BRENDA HASTINGS\nL12@P0: DR. AARON THOMPSON\nL13@P0: (Write-in)\nL14@P0: SAMPLE BALLOT\n"
